<%#
  Email-change-pending modal — the handoff after PATCH /profile/email.

  Opened via $store.<store>.open('email-change-pending', { currentEmail, newEmail }).
  Rendered inside a modal host, which supplies the backdrop, card chrome, scroll
  lock, escape, click-outside and mount animation.

  INFORMATIONAL, not a celebration. Someone changed an address they already had,
  the server held the change and mailed a link to the CURRENT address, and this
  says go and click it. Nothing has changed yet, and the copy leads with that
  rather than burying it.

  It names BOTH addresses because they are the whole point: which inbox to go to,
  and what will happen when they do. Reading "we sent you an email" without
  saying WHERE is the failure this replaces.

  Ported from turf-monster's app/views/modals/_email_change_pending.html.erb,
  which was already built on this engine's own card_header block.

  Single root: it lives inside the host's <template x-if>, so only the outer div
  is top-level here.

  Local: store — Alpine store name this modal is mounted in. Default "modals";
  /profile passes "profileModals" for its page-scoped host.
%>
<% pending_store = local_assigns.fetch(:store, "modals") %>
<div x-data="{ get props() { return ($store.<%= pending_store %>.current() || {}).props || {} } }">
  <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/card_header",
        icon_emoji: "📬",
        title: "Confirm your email change" do %>
    We sent a confirmation link to
    <span class="text-heading font-medium" x-text="props.currentEmail"></span>
    — your current address. Open it to finish changing your email to
    <span class="text-heading font-medium" x-text="props.newEmail"></span>.
    Nothing changes until you do, and the link expires in <%= Studio::EmailChangeToken::TTL / 60 %> minutes.
  <% end %>
  <button @click="$store.<%= pending_store %>.close()"
          class="btn btn-primary btn-lg w-full">Got it</button>
</div>
